WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.767
-[all screaming]
-[thuds]

3
00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:18.310
Is everyone all right?

4
00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.770
Where's Jimmy?

5
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.149
[gasps. sighs]

6
00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:27.611
Oh. man.
this is gonna get everywhere.

7
00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:30.322
Hey. uh...

8
00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:32.991
What are you wearing?

9
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.285
[exclaims] Wait.
what am I wearing?

10
00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:37.246
[announcer]
<i>Well met. champions.</i>

11
00:00:38.205 --> 00:00:40.165
<i>Let the contest begin.</i>

12
00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:41.542
-Contest?
-What was that?

13
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.335
[slurping]

14
00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:46.088
How are my favorite mortals?

15
00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:47.965
Mxy. what's going on?

16
00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:49.216
Oh! [snaps]

17
00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:52.970
I'm getting divorced.

18
00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:54.137
[all] What?

19
00:00:56.932 --> 00:00:58.016
Mxy? why are we here?

20
00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.702
[chuckles] You're cute
when you're anxious.

21
00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.769
Glitzy!

22
00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.732
You called. my former darling?

23
00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:07.859
This is Ms. Gsptlsnz.

24
00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:09.111
You can call me Glitzy.

25
00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:10.696
My soon to be ex-wife.

26
00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.322
Charmed.

27
00:01:12.364 --> 00:01:14.658
-That answered nothing.
-You have a wife?

28
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.159
Ex-wife. Keep up!

29
00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:17.619
Glitzy and I
are untying the knot.

30
00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:19.347
but instead of all that
courtroom business.

31
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:21.790
-our people settle things...
-With a contest?

32
00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:26.086
Yes. Super-brain. a contest.
tournament. games. whatever.

33
00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:29.047
Glitzy and I have each
recruited a team of players.

34
00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:30.340
You're my team.

35
00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:32.217
Gullible Superman.
Jimmy Lamebird.

36
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:35.554
Question Mark Kara.
and Fun Lois.

37
00:01:35.596 --> 00:01:38.140
<i>The teams compete
in a series of challenges.</i>

38
00:01:38.181 --> 00:01:40.892
<i>Each challenge cleared
gets you A. a key</i>

39
00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.270
<i>and B. entry to the next ring.</i>

40
00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:45.606
<i>Whoever's team
collects the most keys</i>

41
00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.149
<i>and gets
to the center ring fastest</i>

42
00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:48.483
<i>determines whether Glitzy or I</i>

43
00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:51.194
<i>get the house. speedboat.
Galaxy. etcetera!</i>

44
00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:53.989
What if we do not
wish to be pawns?

45
00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:54.990
Right?

46
00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:56.575
[laughs hysterically]

47
00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:58.410
Almost forgot.

48
00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:01.747
Lose and you will never see
your precious universe again.

49
00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.332
Sorry. Anything else?

50
00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:05.542
-So we'd be trapped here?
-Forever.

51
00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:07.145
Do you think you will
get away with this?

52
00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:09.921
If we're your team.
then who's Glitzy team?

53
00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.299
[Mxyzptlk] Yes. Yes. Ooh. yes.

54
00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:13.467
And don't worry about it.

55
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.761
We have Superman.

56
00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:18.096
We... We don't have Superman.

57
00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.640
What was that?

58
00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:21.183
I lost my powers.

59
00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.769
You... lost... your...

60
00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:24.852
powers?

61
00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:26.229
[groans] Before my divorce.

62
00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:28.857
I needed Superman.

63
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.611
Clark Kent is useless to me.

64
00:02:32.694 --> 00:02:35.697
[laughs] Embarrassing.

65
00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:41.036
Anyway. it's my great pleasure
to introduce team Glitzy.

66
00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.829
[upbeat rock music playing]

67
00:02:42.913 --> 00:02:45.040
First up. General Lane.

68
00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:46.166
Oh. no.

69
00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:48.960
[Gzptlsnz] That is.
General Lois Lane.

70
00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.295
Oh. no.

71
00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:51.922
[Gzptlsnz] Good Lex Luthor...

72
00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:58.970
Scion Kara from the House of El.

73
00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:01.014
And Flamebird Jimmy.

74
00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:02.891
Oh. that's just me.

75
00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:04.685
Flamebird. [grunts]

76
00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:06.937
[amusing music playing]

77
00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:13.819
Nope. A way cooler me.

78
00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.529
Hey. Hi. excuse me.

79
00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:17.030
I was swindled.

80
00:03:17.114 --> 00:03:19.825
I chose Superman. instead I got
a bumbling. useless.

81
00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:21.493
nearsighted reporter!

82
00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:22.494
Okay. man...

83
00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:24.746
The playing field
must be leveled.

84
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.957
How about no flying allowed?

85
00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:30.043
No. Buyer beware. your fault.

86
00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:32.170
Ruling. please.

87
00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:35.006
[announcer]
<i>The champions shall not fly.</i>

88
00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.092
-Ugh.
-[grunts]

89
00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:39.803
Eat that. love of my life.

90
00:03:40.512 --> 00:03:41.471
[Clark] What's happening?

91
00:03:41.513 --> 00:03:43.724
[Gzptlsnz]
Mxy. I will crush him.

92
00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:50.605
When the big boy says.
"Go." cross the bridge.

93
00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:52.858
get the key.
do it faster than them...

94
00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:55.277
and watch your step.

95
00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:58.238
[announcer] <i>Let the first
challenge commence.</i>

96
00:04:03.118 --> 00:04:04.453
[all panting]

97
00:04:05.036 --> 00:04:06.079
[grunts]

98
00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:09.291
[groans]

99
00:04:14.212 --> 00:04:15.297
[scoffs]

100
00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:18.633
Can you believe the way Glitzy

101
00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:23.305
is trying to get under my skin.
pitting me against her?

102
00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:25.223
It's not like that could
ever be me.

103
00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:27.350
[chuckles nervously] Right?
[exclaims]

104
00:04:27.392 --> 00:04:28.560
[both scream]

105
00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.353
Clark!

106
00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:32.606
[grunting]

107
00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:34.191
[exclaims]

108
00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:35.275
[grunting]

109
00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:38.570
-[screaming]
-Run!

110
00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:40.238
[all panting]

111
00:04:41.239 --> 00:04:42.699
[all screaming]

112
00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:43.867
[all groan]

113
00:04:46.536 --> 00:04:48.914
I'm sorry I wasn't fast enough.

114
00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:50.040
-I just...
-Is that...

115
00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:53.084
A key!

116
00:04:56.046 --> 00:04:58.131
[chuckles] I'll take that.

117
00:04:58.215 --> 00:05:00.467
How about a thank you. team?

118
00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.260
That would imply you
did a good job.

119
00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.012
Hey. we got the key. didn't we?

120
00:05:04.095 --> 00:05:06.223
Just barely. Look at them.

121
00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:09.768
[epic rock music playing]

122
00:05:11.353 --> 00:05:12.854
So? It's a tie.

123
00:05:12.938 --> 00:05:14.606
[screaming] A tie? Pathetic!

124
00:05:14.689 --> 00:05:15.982
You didn't come here to tie.

125
00:05:16.066 --> 00:05:17.859
You came here to win!

126
00:05:17.943 --> 00:05:19.611
Next game.

127
00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:21.321
[all exclaim]

128
00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.406
[all groan]

129
00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:25.283
[groans]

130
00:05:26.034 --> 00:05:27.202
You.

131
00:05:27.244 --> 00:05:30.622
Ladies and ladies. may I present

132
00:05:31.122 --> 00:05:35.210
S'ivaan Mountain.

133
00:05:35.293 --> 00:05:37.337
Your mission. should you
choose to accept it...

134
00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.631
Ha! I jest...
You don't have rights...

135
00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:43.134
is to climb S'ivaan Mountain.

136
00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.386
Whoever gets to the top first

137
00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:46.555
wins this round's
one and only key.

138
00:05:46.638 --> 00:05:49.140
As you ascend.
the mountain will sink

139
00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.518
into the Manticore trench.

140
00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:52.829
Anyway. if you're
too slow or slip.

141
00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:53.871
you'll meet the Manticore.

142
00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:56.898
Last team to make it
to the top loses.

143
00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.112
This is the boy challenge.

144
00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.322
These are portal pieces.

145
00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:07.158
Find them. put them together.
make a portal. leave it.

146
00:06:07.242 --> 00:06:08.994
Whoever does it first wins.

147
00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:12.163
-That's it?
-Yes! Just win.

148
00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:13.665
[Clark groans] Man!

149
00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:16.376
[Lois panting]

150
00:06:16.459 --> 00:06:18.420
The mountain does not feel
like it is sinking.

151
00:06:18.503 --> 00:06:19.629
This is unchallenging.

152
00:06:19.671 --> 00:06:23.925
[panting] Yep.
very unchallenging.

153
00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:27.846
Lois Lane. is it my fate
to become like... that?

154
00:06:29.014 --> 00:06:32.183
Her? [scoffs] I mean.
you were like that.

155
00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:35.186
Look. I've met
a whole league of Lois-es.

156
00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.897
These other selves mean nothing.

157
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.481
Oh. now it is sinking.

158
00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.066
Go. go. go!

159
00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.363
Get to the top.

160
00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.032
Only one of us needs to win.

161
00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:50.535
[panting. groans]

162
00:06:50.952 --> 00:06:51.995
Are you crazy?

163
00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:55.081
[screams]

164
00:07:00.295 --> 00:07:02.172
Do you think
our Lois-es are okay?

165
00:07:02.213 --> 00:07:04.716
[scoffs. groans] Whoa!

166
00:07:06.551 --> 00:07:08.219
[suspenseful music playing]

167
00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:13.850
You must be cautious.
Other Kara.

168
00:07:19.689 --> 00:07:21.608
[creature growling]

169
00:07:23.026 --> 00:07:24.486
Okay. let's move.

170
00:07:26.738 --> 00:07:28.573
Shouldn't we hide out somewhere?

171
00:07:28.615 --> 00:07:30.659
I'm finding a way out.

172
00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.702
We can barely see.
We don't know the area

173
00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:35.205
and there's a beast
trying to hunt us.

174
00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:37.082
Lanes are doers.
not complainers.

175
00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:38.375
I'm not complaining.

176
00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:40.251
But maybe we
should wait where we fell in.

177
00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.586
What if our Karas need us?

178
00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.421
If they join us. they failed.

179
00:07:43.505 --> 00:07:45.423
They can handle
the consequences.

180
00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:47.842
Wow. we are so different.

181
00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:51.262
Hmm. let me guess. Mom died.
Dad was distant.

182
00:07:51.346 --> 00:07:53.014
All you wanted was
work. work. work.

183
00:07:53.098 --> 00:07:56.059
But instead you find
the "super man" of your dreams.

184
00:07:56.101 --> 00:07:59.938
learn the meaning of friendship
and have a real swell time.

185
00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.272
That was me too.

186
00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:04.609
But then Clark lost his powers
and... And then his life.

187
00:08:05.402 --> 00:08:06.820
So go ahead and judge me.

188
00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:09.864
but the line between us isn't
as thick as you think it is.

189
00:08:11.992 --> 00:08:13.618
[growling]

190
00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.660
Ahhh!

191
00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:16.663
-[dramatic music playing]
-[growling]

192
00:08:19.958 --> 00:08:21.126
[music speeds up]

193
00:08:23.128 --> 00:08:24.421
[grunting]

194
00:08:24.462 --> 00:08:25.588
Ahhh!

195
00:08:26.798 --> 00:08:27.799
Why?

196
00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.135
No!

197
00:08:30.927 --> 00:08:31.970
Kara!

198
00:08:40.145 --> 00:08:41.354
You cheated.

199
00:08:41.438 --> 00:08:43.648
No. I won.

200
00:08:43.732 --> 00:08:45.650
You had the chance
to do the same.

201
00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:47.652
and you wanted to.

202
00:08:47.736 --> 00:08:50.655
Do not lie to yourself. Kara.

203
00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:52.198
This is who we are.

204
00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.165
A-ha!

205
00:09:01.332 --> 00:09:03.793
Check it out. Clark...
and others.

206
00:09:03.835 --> 00:09:05.712
One more down. one more to...

207
00:09:05.795 --> 00:09:07.422
-Hey!
-It's ours.

208
00:09:07.505 --> 00:09:08.631
It's clearly orange.

209
00:09:08.673 --> 00:09:10.341
[stuttering] It's hard to tell.

210
00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:11.843
Anyone could have
made that mistake.

211
00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:15.221
I wonder how many of our pieces
you may have stolen by mistake.

212
00:09:15.305 --> 00:09:17.766
-Look. I don't think...
-Are you saying I'm lying?

213
00:09:17.849 --> 00:09:20.643
I'm suggesting
there may be foul play. yes.

214
00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:22.020
[Other Jimmy] Hey. let's not...

215
00:09:22.103 --> 00:09:24.355
You'd only think like that
if you were doing it yourself.

216
00:09:24.439 --> 00:09:27.233
Okay. Lex.
it was an honest mistake.

217
00:09:27.317 --> 00:09:28.818
but to make everyone
feel better.

218
00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.695
why don't I look for pieces
with you.

219
00:09:30.737 --> 00:09:33.698
And Jimmy. you can go with...
Jimmy.

220
00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:37.452
So we can all be sure
everyone's playing fair. Deal?

221
00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:38.828
-Very well.
-Fine.

222
00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:41.539
All right. Jimmy. time.
Let's go.

223
00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:42.957
[Jimmy] Just be cool. man.

224
00:09:46.795 --> 00:09:50.465
So. your world seems like a...
interesting place. [chuckles]

225
00:09:50.548 --> 00:09:52.050
How'd you all end up together?

226
00:09:52.133 --> 00:09:53.676
No more Superman.

227
00:09:53.718 --> 00:09:54.677
This one's yours.

228
00:09:54.719 --> 00:09:56.596
What? Oh. uh. thank you.

229
00:09:56.679 --> 00:09:59.682
What happened to Superman
in your world?

230
00:09:59.724 --> 00:10:01.142
Mistakes were made.

231
00:10:01.226 --> 00:10:03.103
I made a mistake.

232
00:10:03.186 --> 00:10:05.647
And with Superman gone.
we didn't stand a chance

233
00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:06.856
when the hunger dogs came.

234
00:10:06.898 --> 00:10:08.650
Everything changed
for the worse.

235
00:10:08.733 --> 00:10:10.276
And we did what we had to.

236
00:10:11.402 --> 00:10:13.196
Are you helping or what?

237
00:10:13.238 --> 00:10:14.280
Right. right.

238
00:10:16.574 --> 00:10:18.910
Okay. that suit is awesome.

239
00:10:18.993 --> 00:10:20.078
I know. right?

240
00:10:20.161 --> 00:10:22.914
Kara and Lois can be
so negative sometimes.

241
00:10:22.956 --> 00:10:25.250
But. hey. if the hunger
dogs hadn't invaded.

242
00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:26.835
I wouldn't have this sick suit.

243
00:10:26.918 --> 00:10:29.963
-Uh. the what invaded?
-Always silver lining.

244
00:10:30.588 --> 00:10:31.589
sick suit.

245
00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:33.424
Lex is good now.
and we're all as close

246
00:10:33.508 --> 00:10:35.260
as we were before Clark died.

247
00:10:35.343 --> 00:10:36.469
Clark died?

248
00:10:36.553 --> 00:10:38.513
-Yep. just three best friends.
-[bones cracking]

249
00:10:38.596 --> 00:10:40.640
We're all doing great.

250
00:10:40.723 --> 00:10:41.808
That doesn't sound great.

251
00:10:41.891 --> 00:10:44.102
Everything is exactly the same.

252
00:10:44.644 --> 00:10:46.771
Well... except...

253
00:10:48.565 --> 00:10:51.401
I'm a superhero now!
Pew. pew. Pew.

254
00:10:51.442 --> 00:10:52.628
-Right. Right.
-Pew. pew. pew. pew.

255
00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:54.445
But aren't you
upset or worried about...

256
00:10:54.529 --> 00:10:55.864
Boo! Boo-hoo!

257
00:10:55.947 --> 00:10:58.032
Working together. Feelings?

258
00:10:58.116 --> 00:11:00.785
[fake laughing] This is boring.

259
00:11:00.827 --> 00:11:02.954
The girls are done already.

260
00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.624
Release the Hell Hippos.

261
00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:07.917
[both] The what?

262
00:11:10.587 --> 00:11:12.088
[roaring]

263
00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.010
Do you have the last piece?

264
00:11:17.093 --> 00:11:18.136
No. do you?

265
00:11:18.636 --> 00:11:19.846
Looking for this?

266
00:11:19.929 --> 00:11:22.724
Oh. [chuckles] Yeah.
There's only one.

267
00:11:22.807 --> 00:11:25.310
Give it to us.
We're on your team.

268
00:11:25.393 --> 00:11:26.728
Team-shmeam.

269
00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:29.147
It's more fun
watching you scream.

270
00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:32.483
[both groan]

271
00:11:34.819 --> 00:11:37.113
Jimmy. give Lex the piece.

272
00:11:37.155 --> 00:11:38.406
What? No.

273
00:11:38.489 --> 00:11:39.741
Jimmy. I'm not Superman.

274
00:11:39.782 --> 00:11:42.452
I... Give it to him
or you'll all die!

275
00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:44.078
[grunts]

276
00:11:50.043 --> 00:11:51.502
[roaring]

277
00:11:52.337 --> 00:11:53.338
No.

278
00:11:54.505 --> 00:11:55.715
I'm so sorry. Jimmy.

279
00:11:55.798 --> 00:11:57.342
[both scream]

280
00:11:58.843 --> 00:12:00.136
[Lois] Clark.

281
00:12:00.178 --> 00:12:01.822
-Are you guys okay?
-What happened to you?

282
00:12:01.846 --> 00:12:02.847
[both] We almost died.

283
00:12:02.931 --> 00:12:04.432
Yeah. I know. Us. too.

284
00:12:04.515 --> 00:12:06.351
Oh. you're fine. Grow up.

285
00:12:06.434 --> 00:12:08.561
Also. you're losing. losers!

286
00:12:08.645 --> 00:12:10.939
And another one for Glitzy.

287
00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:14.984
Good work.

288
00:12:15.026 --> 00:12:18.363
Do you people
even want a universe?

289
00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:19.697
Mmm. could be worse.

290
00:12:19.781 --> 00:12:22.158
At least he didn't
let the Hell Hippos get us.

291
00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.952
Hell Hippos? Wait!

292
00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:27.580
Glitzy also got us away
before the Manticore attacked.

293
00:12:27.664 --> 00:12:29.082
Why are they saving us?

294
00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.336
[wind blowing]

295
00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.090
Okay. dummies.

296
00:12:37.173 --> 00:12:38.716
This is a maze.

297
00:12:38.758 --> 00:12:39.884
All you gotta do this time

298
00:12:39.926 --> 00:12:42.720
is choose your one true path
and follow it.

299
00:12:42.804 --> 00:12:45.306
And how do we know
which path is right?

300
00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.724
Pick the path you like best.

301
00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:50.311
Just don't let
the trail go cold. [laughs]

302
00:12:50.395 --> 00:12:51.437
Okay. bye.

303
00:12:51.521 --> 00:12:54.148
[groans] One day.
I will crush him.

304
00:12:55.316 --> 00:12:56.359
Humanely.

305
00:12:57.235 --> 00:12:58.278
[exclaims]

306
00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:00.905
-Ahhh!
-[Clark] Ahhh!

307
00:13:02.532 --> 00:13:03.616
[panting]

308
00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:04.742
Clark!

309
00:13:05.243 --> 00:13:06.286
Lois!

310
00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:16.004
[grunting]

311
00:13:16.671 --> 00:13:17.714
[sighs]

312
00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:20.633
Lois.

313
00:13:22.427 --> 00:13:23.469
What?

314
00:13:33.563 --> 00:13:35.273
I used to be Superman.

315
00:13:37.233 --> 00:13:38.276
Who am I now?

316
00:13:46.367 --> 00:13:48.286
Are you still my path?

317
00:13:59.922 --> 00:14:02.467
Great. more Lois-es?

318
00:14:03.301 --> 00:14:04.344
Nope.

319
00:14:05.303 --> 00:14:06.346
Nah.

320
00:14:07.472 --> 00:14:08.514
No.

321
00:14:10.141 --> 00:14:13.186
Not seeing any
"one true paths" in here.

322
00:14:14.562 --> 00:14:16.606
[amusing music playing]

323
00:14:16.647 --> 00:14:18.024
I remember this.

324
00:14:19.734 --> 00:14:21.152
[music intensifies]

325
00:14:21.235 --> 00:14:22.445
No.

326
00:14:22.487 --> 00:14:23.613
No. it can't.

327
00:14:25.656 --> 00:14:26.657
No.

328
00:14:29.911 --> 00:14:31.287
This can't be real.

329
00:14:32.914 --> 00:14:35.166
This... can't... be...

330
00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.170
[music intensifies. stops]

331
00:14:39.212 --> 00:14:41.672
[Jimmy] I. uh.
talked to Flamebird Jimmy.

332
00:14:41.756 --> 00:14:43.758
He's pretending
that everything's okay.

333
00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:44.967
that it'll all work out

334
00:14:45.009 --> 00:14:47.095
when it's falling apart
in front of him.

335
00:14:47.929 --> 00:14:51.015
Perhaps that is our only path.

336
00:14:51.057 --> 00:14:54.727
No. look. I haven't been
a good friend. Kara.

337
00:14:54.811 --> 00:14:56.896
I haven't been a good anything.

338
00:14:56.979 --> 00:14:58.481
I still think
you deserve better.

339
00:14:58.523 --> 00:15:01.234
So I am going to be better.

340
00:15:02.068 --> 00:15:03.277
I need to change.

341
00:15:04.195 --> 00:15:05.238
[shatters]

342
00:15:06.447 --> 00:15:07.365
Say that again.

343
00:15:07.448 --> 00:15:08.658
Oh. that I need to change.

344
00:15:08.699 --> 00:15:10.118
And I... I mean it. Kara.

345
00:15:10.201 --> 00:15:12.703
-I know...
-Hush. That is it.

346
00:15:12.787 --> 00:15:14.247
When I saw Scion Kara.

347
00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.707
I feared that brainiac
was right about me.

348
00:15:16.791 --> 00:15:19.419
that my one true self
was like him.

349
00:15:20.545 --> 00:15:22.046
But I am not one thing.

350
00:15:22.088 --> 00:15:24.173
We are all creatures of change.

351
00:15:24.215 --> 00:15:26.509
We can become anything.

352
00:15:26.551 --> 00:15:27.552
Jimmy Flamebird.

353
00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:30.555
this game is a trick.

354
00:15:30.596 --> 00:15:34.225
We decide who we are every day.

355
00:15:34.267 --> 00:15:36.811
There is no one true path.

356
00:15:36.894 --> 00:15:39.730
The future is ours to shape.

357
00:15:39.772 --> 00:15:41.941
[shattering]

358
00:15:46.779 --> 00:15:48.573
Wait. what happened?

359
00:15:48.656 --> 00:15:50.825
Anything can happen. Lois Lane.

360
00:15:50.908 --> 00:15:52.910
There is no one true path.

361
00:15:52.994 --> 00:15:54.054
That was the solution all...

362
00:15:54.078 --> 00:15:55.663
-Yea. real moving.
-Hey!

363
00:15:55.746 --> 00:15:57.123
What happened to the other team?

364
00:15:57.206 --> 00:16:00.835
Oh. them. One could say
they missed the mark.

365
00:16:00.918 --> 00:16:02.587
[giggles] Bunch of drips. huh!

366
00:16:02.628 --> 00:16:05.673
[chuckles] Total wash. [gasps]
Wait. wait! I got more.

367
00:16:07.425 --> 00:16:08.426
Not so fast.

368
00:16:11.929 --> 00:16:13.389
There's just one game left.

369
00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:16.809
And Mama's gonna get that house.

370
00:16:16.893 --> 00:16:18.311
[doorbell rings]

371
00:16:23.983 --> 00:16:26.402
[Gzptlsnz] Aw. hamster balls.

372
00:16:26.444 --> 00:16:27.945
Can we keep them?

373
00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:29.572
You always do this.

374
00:16:29.614 --> 00:16:32.283
You get attached. they die.
you're sad.

375
00:16:32.366 --> 00:16:34.952
My empathy makes me likable.

376
00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:37.663
First ball through
the obstacle course wins.

377
00:16:37.747 --> 00:16:40.082
-Ready. set...
-[Lois] Wait!

378
00:16:40.124 --> 00:16:41.626
Things aren't adding up.

379
00:16:41.709 --> 00:16:43.961
She's right. For example.
it hasn't seemed to matter

380
00:16:44.045 --> 00:16:46.631
who wins the keys
as long as they're being won.

381
00:16:46.714 --> 00:16:49.634
Exactly. Like. why did we
both win the first game?

382
00:16:49.717 --> 00:16:51.719
And why do all the keys
go to the same place

383
00:16:51.802 --> 00:16:53.471
no matter who wins them?

384
00:16:53.554 --> 00:16:55.139
And who is that guy?

385
00:16:55.181 --> 00:16:56.766
[thunder rumbling]

386
00:16:56.807 --> 00:16:59.936
Beings of your dimension
couldn't possibly understand...

387
00:16:59.977 --> 00:17:04.232
[groans] No... more... games!

388
00:17:04.899 --> 00:17:07.109
Very well. since you insist.

389
00:17:07.151 --> 00:17:10.488
That structure over there
is the cosmic anvil.

390
00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:13.115
[Gzptlsnz] A device that can
reshape a universe.

391
00:17:13.157 --> 00:17:15.117
the keys unlock its power.

392
00:17:15.159 --> 00:17:16.327
We needed you lovely mortals

393
00:17:16.369 --> 00:17:18.621
to retrieve the keys
because. well...

394
00:17:18.663 --> 00:17:20.081
There's a curse

395
00:17:20.122 --> 00:17:23.209
that prevents certain immortals
from unlocking it.

396
00:17:23.292 --> 00:17:26.045
-Okay? Happy now?
-[Kara] No!

397
00:17:26.128 --> 00:17:27.568
That's why we've been
doing all this?

398
00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.340
[whispering indistinctly]

399
00:17:30.174 --> 00:17:31.634
How about some incentive?

400
00:17:31.676 --> 00:17:34.512
The winners get
to reshape their universe

401
00:17:34.595 --> 00:17:37.431
however they want.

402
00:17:37.515 --> 00:17:39.100
Fun Lois. lean in.

403
00:17:39.141 --> 00:17:41.185
You could pick
whatever future you want.

404
00:17:41.227 --> 00:17:45.189
Clark. you could get
your powers back. Mmm. mmm?

405
00:17:45.231 --> 00:17:46.857
You could bring Clark back.

406
00:17:46.899 --> 00:17:48.401
Don't you mean Superman?

407
00:17:48.484 --> 00:17:49.694
No.

408
00:17:49.777 --> 00:17:52.572
Superman losing his powers
was... difficult.

409
00:17:52.655 --> 00:17:55.866
But when we lost Clark.
we lost... everything.

410
00:17:55.908 --> 00:17:57.618
[somber music playing]

411
00:17:58.202 --> 00:18:00.621
Okay. let's play.

412
00:18:00.663 --> 00:18:03.666
Wait. guys. we... We...
We can't just trust Mxy

413
00:18:03.708 --> 00:18:05.001
to deliver on these promises.

414
00:18:05.042 --> 00:18:08.004
Maybe the reward
is worth the risk.

415
00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:09.714
Well. what is the risk?

416
00:18:09.755 --> 00:18:11.299
What happens to the losers?

417
00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:15.803
The losers get turned into
a gift for my beloved wife.

418
00:18:15.886 --> 00:18:18.598
Maybe a Ficus. Huh.

419
00:18:18.681 --> 00:18:19.849
[both] Beloved wife?

420
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:22.393
[laughs] Okay. you got us.

421
00:18:22.476 --> 00:18:25.313
This is a date. not a divorce.

422
00:18:25.354 --> 00:18:29.609
Just some good old fashioned
role play. to spice things up.

423
00:18:29.692 --> 00:18:31.402
Oh. we do have fun.

424
00:18:31.444 --> 00:18:32.945
-[kissing]
-[all groaning]

425
00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:34.655
So what do you say?

426
00:18:34.739 --> 00:18:35.990
We can't play their game?

427
00:18:36.073 --> 00:18:37.950
Don't listen to team Ficus.

428
00:18:38.034 --> 00:18:39.410
They're just afraid to lose.

429
00:18:39.452 --> 00:18:42.038
Look. I've dealt
with Mxy before.

430
00:18:42.079 --> 00:18:43.247
and if he unlocks that thing.

431
00:18:43.331 --> 00:18:45.291
whatever he's gonna do with it
will not be good.

432
00:18:45.374 --> 00:18:47.418
What do you mean.
"Dealt with him before?"

433
00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:50.671
Uh. what interest would
an immortal have in a reporter?

434
00:18:50.755 --> 00:18:51.797
[chuckles] No offense.

435
00:18:54.925 --> 00:18:56.802
What is. uh...

436
00:18:56.886 --> 00:18:58.220
I... I don't understand.

437
00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:02.683
It... It... It's... you.

438
00:19:03.517 --> 00:19:05.936
Did everyone know this but me?

439
00:19:05.978 --> 00:19:07.480
-Yes. hello.
-Yeah.

440
00:19:08.606 --> 00:19:09.690
[groans]

441
00:19:09.732 --> 00:19:11.817
I regret not listening
to Superman when...

442
00:19:12.401 --> 00:19:13.778
When I had the chance.

443
00:19:13.819 --> 00:19:15.946
I'm not gonna make
the same mistake twice.

444
00:19:18.449 --> 00:19:20.326
[ticking]

445
00:19:20.409 --> 00:19:24.455
Hey. play now or I'll give you
something to regret.

446
00:19:25.623 --> 00:19:26.707
We aren't playing.

447
00:19:26.749 --> 00:19:30.836
Let me get this through
your thick skulls!

448
00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:36.008
Defy me. and I will crush you
like the bugs you are.

449
00:19:36.092 --> 00:19:39.261
Play or die!

450
00:19:39.303 --> 00:19:41.389
Well. then we die.

451
00:19:41.472 --> 00:19:43.683
-Clark. what are you doing?
-Yeah. buddy.

452
00:19:43.766 --> 00:19:45.017
Go ahead. Mxy.

453
00:19:45.101 --> 00:19:47.520
There's nothing
stopping you. right?

454
00:19:47.603 --> 00:19:48.854
[growling]

455
00:19:52.566 --> 00:19:57.405
[announcer] <i>The hour has come
and the contest has no victor.</i>

456
00:19:57.488 --> 00:20:00.324
<i>My seal remains unbroken.</i>

457
00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:03.160
<i>Farewell. champions!</i>

458
00:20:03.244 --> 00:20:04.704
<i>Burn in hell. Mxy.</i>

459
00:20:04.787 --> 00:20:07.498
-Oh. no!
-No!

460
00:20:09.709 --> 00:20:11.001
I do not understand.

461
00:20:11.085 --> 00:20:12.837
Those were hourglasses...

462
00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:14.839
showing how much time
was left in the game.

463
00:20:14.922 --> 00:20:18.384
-And you knew it was game over.
-Game over.

464
00:20:18.467 --> 00:20:21.095
Not bad for a bumbling. useless.

465
00:20:21.178 --> 00:20:23.180
nearsighted reporter. huh. Mxy?

466
00:20:23.264 --> 00:20:25.558
No. my anvil!

467
00:20:25.641 --> 00:20:31.272
[groaning] Why do you people
always ruin it? [crying]

468
00:20:31.355 --> 00:20:33.941
Why. why. why. why?

469
00:20:34.024 --> 00:20:36.485
Ugh. Oh. in front of
the mortals?

470
00:20:36.527 --> 00:20:38.654
I can't watch this. I'm out.

471
00:20:38.696 --> 00:20:40.072
Glitzy. wait!

472
00:20:40.156 --> 00:20:41.449
It was just role play. baby.

473
00:20:41.532 --> 00:20:45.161
Baby. it was just role play.

474
00:20:45.202 --> 00:20:46.912
Hey. you never
answered my question.

475
00:20:46.996 --> 00:20:48.122
Who is that guy?

476
00:20:48.205 --> 00:20:49.874
[thunder rumbling]

477
00:20:49.915 --> 00:20:52.001
A sore loser.

478
00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:56.380
-[all] Whoa!
-[all thud]

479
00:20:56.422 --> 00:20:58.883
Oh. my sweet tailored suit.

480
00:20:58.966 --> 00:21:00.968
[calm music playing]

481
00:21:04.221 --> 00:21:05.806
[breathing heavily]

482
00:21:08.768 --> 00:21:11.145
[chuckles] Uh. hey. there. stranger.

483
00:21:11.228 --> 00:21:13.439
[chuckles] Fancy
meeting you here.

484
00:21:13.522 --> 00:21:16.609
Yeah. I decided to wake up a
little earlier. clear my head.

485
00:21:16.692 --> 00:21:19.612
Same. I knew there was
a reason we were together.

486
00:21:19.695 --> 00:21:23.783
Yeah. I think. uh. I actually
feel better now than before.

487
00:21:23.866 --> 00:21:25.451
Whatever that was.

488
00:21:25.534 --> 00:21:28.829
I think I'm starting
to like Clark Kent.

489
00:21:28.913 --> 00:21:30.247
Maybe he's enough.

490
00:21:30.289 --> 00:21:31.332
Of course he is.

491
00:21:31.415 --> 00:21:33.042
[imperceptible]

492
00:21:34.293 --> 00:21:35.293
But how are you?

493
00:21:35.336 --> 00:21:37.838
I'm... kinda shaken. honestly.

494
00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:40.549
I thought I knew
what our future was gonna be.

495
00:21:40.591 --> 00:21:42.760
But now it feels like
we can't keep up.

496
00:21:42.802 --> 00:21:46.597
Like we keep fighting
against these terrible futures.

497
00:21:46.639 --> 00:21:49.308
They're not terrible. Lois.
They're just...

498
00:21:57.066 --> 00:21:58.108
different.

499
00:21:59.068 --> 00:22:01.445
[dramatic music playing]

500
00:22:04.073 --> 00:22:05.449
[closing theme music playing]

500
00:22:06.305 --> 00:23:06.528
